1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:13,000
Welcome to Ofrenda: Yaadon ka Diya — a virtual remembrance altar bridging Día de los Muertos with the Indian tradition of lighting a Diya.

2
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:24,000
Built for Week 4 of the Dev.to Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge, exploring "Ghost in the Machine" as a compassionate mirror of memories.

3
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:34,500
Notice our privacy pledge: "Sab kuch aapke device par. Koi account nahi." Everything stays strictly on your personal device.

4
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:48,000
Let us honor Dadi Savitri Devi: we enter her favorite foods like warm jalebi and chai, her melody "Lag Ja Gale", and Sunday morning memories.

5
00:00:48,200 --> 00:01:00,500
Now, we click "Light the Diya". The sacred flame awakens, and an open-weight AI model begins streaming a warm remembrance letter in natural Hinglish.

6
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:13,000
Under strict AI rules, the model never invents facts, uses zero clichés, and keeps the tribute concentrated and tender.

7
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:27,000
Our three-tier altar lights up: Level 1 holds her golden portrait, Level 2 presents her food offerings, and Level 3 gathers melodies, extra diyas, and marigolds.

8
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:38,000
With a single click, you can download the entire glowing altar as a high-resolution PNG and export the letter to a text file.

9
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:53,000
Why open models? Because sacred family memories, tears, and private recipes should never feed closed corporate APIs. Open innovation keeps love eternal.
